{"id":"QB-261125-5RCG","title":"Thu Thao · 25/11 · Algebra, Geometry and Trigonometry","student":"Thu Thao","questions":[{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-US-A-M2-Q14","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-US-A-M2-Q14","label":"1","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"During a trip, a car traveled a total of 480 miles on city roads and highways and used a total of 16 gallons of gas. The car traveled an average of 28 miles per gallon of gas on city roads and 34 miles per gallon of gas on highways. Which system of equations represents this situation, where $c$ is the number of miles the car traveled on city roads and $h$ is the number of miles the car traveled on highways?","options":{"A":"$c+h=16,\\quad\\frac{c}{28}+\\frac{h}{34}=480$","B":"$c+h=16,\\quad28c+34h=480$","C":"$c+h=480,\\quad\\frac{c}{28}+\\frac{h}{34}=16$","D":"$c+h=480,\\quad28c+34h=16$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-US-A-M1-Q18","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-US-A-M1-Q18","label":"2","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"In the figure, lines $r$ and $s$ are parallel and line $t$ intersects both lines. If $a=4k+57$ and $b=\\dfrac{k}{4}+55$, what is the value of $c$?","figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Two parallel vertical lines r (left) and s (right) are crossed by a line t that runs from upper left to lower right. At line r: a° is the angle between the upward part of r and the part of t that goes down to the right. At line s: b° is the angle between the upward part of s and the part of t that goes up to the left; c° is the angle between that same part of t and the downward part of s (b and c are both on the left of s)."}]},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M2-Q18","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M2-Q18","label":"3","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Triangles FGH and JKL are congruent. In triangle FGH, FG = 2GH, FG = 28, and FH = 29. In triangle JKL, JK = 2KL. What is the length of segment JL?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M1-Q06","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M1-Q06","label":"4","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"System of equations:<br><br>$3x = 2 + 8y$ $-3x = -5 + 8y$<br><br>What is the value of $6x$?","options":{"A":"$\\frac{7}{2}$","B":"$7$","C":"$14$","D":"$21$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M2-Q21","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M2-Q21","label":"5","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"During hibernation, American black bears do not eat or replenish calories. A certain black bear weighed 324 pounds when entering hibernation and lost weight at a mean rate of 0.8 pounds per day. At this rate, how many days after entering hibernation would the black bear weigh 260 pounds?","options":{"A":"52","B":"64","C":"80","D":"208"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-A-M2-Q17","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-A-M2-Q17","label":"6","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$y=5x+28$<br>$y=5x+38$<br>How many solutions does the given system of equations have?","options":{"A":"Zero","B":"Exactly one","C":"Exactly two","D":"Infinitely many"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M2-Q01","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M2-Q01","label":"7","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$9x-94=y$<br><br>$10x=110$<br><br>The solution to the given system of equations is $(x,y)$. What is the value of $y$?","options":{"A":"94","B":"11","C":"10","D":"5"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-B-M2-Q19","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-B-M2-Q19","label":"8","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A right square pyramid has a height of $11$ centimeters (cm). A second right square pyramid has a height of $22$ centimeters. The area of the bases of each of the two pyramids is $100$ cm$^2$. Which of the following is closest to the difference in the surface area of the second pyramid and the surface area of the first pyramid, in cm$^2$?","options":{"A":"$209$","B":"$220$","C":"$367$","D":"$551$"}},{"id":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q118","ref":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q118","label":"9","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The base of a right rectangular pyramid has a length of $27$ centimeters and a width of $7$ centimeters. The height of this pyramid is $5$ centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of this pyramid?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025DEC-INT-A-M2-Q08","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025DEC-INT-A-M2-Q08","label":"10","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$0.10x + 0.20y = 0.17(x + y)$<br><br>The equation gives a volume $x$, in gallons, of a 10% saltwater solution that could be mixed with a volume $y$, in gallons, of a 20% saltwater solution to produce a 17% saltwater solution. According to this equation, what volume, in gallons, of the 20% saltwater solution could be mixed with 75.0 gallons of the 10% saltwater solution to produce a 17% saltwater solution? (Assume that the volume of the mixture is the sum of the volumes of the two solutions before they were mixed.)"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-B-M2-Q13","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-B-M2-Q13","label":"11","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A linear function $L$ satisfies $L(4)=19$ and $L(-2)=-5$. An exponential function $E$ is defined by $E(x)=3\\cdot2^{cx}$, where $c$ is a positive constant. If the graphs of $y=L(x)$ and $y=E(x)$ intersect at the point $(2,k)$, what is the value of $k$?","options":{"A":"2","B":"6","C":"11","D":"12"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-INT-A-M1-Q22","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-INT-A-M1-Q22","label":"12","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"For a particular car, the linear function $f$ gives the predicted power, in brake horsepower (bhp), for engine speeds between $1{,}000$ revolutions per minute (rpm) and $6{,}000$ rpm. According to this function, the car's predicted power is $600$ bhp at an engine speed of $4{,}500$ rpm. The equation $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{7}(x-a)+228$ defines $f$, where $x$ is the engine speed, in rpm, and $a$ is a constant. What is the value of $a$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q01","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q01","label":"13","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $v(t)=3t+60$ gives the volume of water, in liters, in a tank being filled by a hose $t$ minutes after the hose was turned on. Which of the following is the best interpretation of $60$ in this context?","options":{"A":"The volume of water in the tank increases at a rate of 60 liters per minute.","B":"The tank holds a maximum of 60 liters.","C":"It takes 60 hours to fill the tank completely.","D":"There were 60 liters of water in the tank when the hose was turned on."}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q02","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q02","label":"14","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"In $\\Delta ABC$, the sum of the measures of $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$ is $159.5^\\circ$. What is the measure of $\\angle C$?","options":{"A":"$20.5^\\circ$","B":"$90^\\circ$","C":"$110.5^\\circ$","D":"$180^\\circ$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M2-Q13","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M2-Q13","label":"15","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$16x-20y=6y+8$<br>$ty=8x+\\frac15$<br><br>In the given system of equations, $t$ is a constant. If the system has no solution, what is the value of $t$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-D-M2-Q20","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-D-M2-Q20","label":"16","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The length of a rectangle's diagonal is $\\sqrt{34}$, and the length of one of the rectangle's sides is $5$. What is the perimeter of the rectangle?","options":{"A":"$34$","B":"$16$","C":"$15$","D":"$8$"}},{"id":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q29","ref":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q29","label":"17","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The roofs on the buildings of a public garden are designed to allow water to drain into the garden. The table shows the relationship between the area $x$, in square feet, of a roof and the amount of water $f(x)$, in gallons, drained from the roof into the garden over a certain period of time.\n\nArea (square feet): 2,400, 3,600, 4,800; Water (gallons): 4,320, 6,480, 8,640\n\nWhich equation could define $f$?","options":{"A":"$f(x) = 0.6x$","B":"$f(x) = 1.8x$","C":"$f(x) = 2,160.0x$","D":"$f(x) = 4,320.0x$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-INT-B-M2-Q13","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-INT-B-M2-Q13","label":"18","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A beekeeper's initial observation of the population of a certain bee colony was $1,800$ bees. The beekeeper set a goal to increase the population to $3,300$ bees. The beekeeper uses a model that predicts the population of this bee colony begins at $1,800$ and increases by $120$ bees per week in the first two weeks after the initial observation, and then increases by $180$ bees per week until the beekeeper's goal is reached. According to this model, at the end of week $w$ after the initial observation, where $w > 2$, which of the following functions gives the predicted number of bees still needed to reach the beekeeper's goal?","options":{"A":"$p(w) = 3,300 - 180w$","B":"$p(w) = 3,180 + 180w$","C":"$p(w) = 1,620 - 180w$","D":"$p(w) = -120 + 180w$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-C-M2-Q19","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-C-M2-Q19","label":"19","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"In the $xy$-plane, line $k$ has a slope of $\\frac{6}{13}$, an $x$-intercept of $(-6, 0)$, and a $y$-intercept of $(0, p)$. What is the value of $p$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q20","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q20","label":"20","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Line $k$ contains the points $(-3, 60)$, $(v, 0)$, and $(5, 76)$. What is the value of $v$?"},{"id":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q96","ref":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q96","label":"21","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"What is the slope of the graph of $y = \\dfrac{1}{3}(26x + 11) + 9x$ in the $xy$-plane?","options":{"A":"$\\dfrac{26}{3}$","B":"$\\dfrac{53}{3}$","C":"$26$","D":"$35$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M1-Q08","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M1-Q08","label":"22","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $f(x) = 43.50 - 0.28x$ gives a person's estimated grip strength, in kilograms, $x$ years after the person's grip strength was first measured. Based on the function, what is this person's estimated grip strength, in kilograms, 32.50 years after the person's grip strength was first measured?","options":{"A":"10.72","B":"34.40","C":"43.50","D":"52.60"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-B-M1-Q22","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-B-M1-Q22","label":"23","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"For two acute angles $X$ and $Y$, the measure of angle $Y$ is $24^\\circ$ and $\\dfrac{\\sin X}{\\cos Y}=1$. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle $X$?","options":{"A":"$24$","B":"$45$","C":"$66$","D":"$69$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M1-Q07","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026AUG-INT-C-M1-Q07","label":"24","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The graph of function f is shown, where y = f(x). Which of the following is the best interpretation of the graph?","options":{"A":"The value of x is 4.25 more than 50 times the value of f(x).","B":"The value of x is 50 more than 4.25 times the value of f(x).","C":"The value of f(x) is 4.25 more than 50 times the value of x.","D":"The value of f(x) is 50 more than 4.25 times the value of x."},"figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Coordinate plane with x-axis labelled x (marks at 5, 10, 15, 20) and y-axis labelled y (marks at 10 to 80). A single straight line segment starts at (0, 50) on the y-axis and rises to the right, ending near x = 5.5, y = 85."}]},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAR-US-C-M1-Q15","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAR-US-C-M1-Q15","label":"25","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$(x+5)^2+(y+8)^2=15^2$<br><br>In the $xy$-plane, the graph of the given equation is a circle. What is the length of a radius of this circle?","options":{"A":"$\\sqrt{15}$","B":"$\\frac{15}{2}$","C":"15","D":"$15^2$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q09","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q09","label":"26","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$$\\begin{array}{|l|c|}\\hline \\text{x} & \\text{y} \\\\ \\hline -12 & 76 \\\\ \\hline -6 & 52 \\\\ \\hline 6 & 4 \\\\ \\hline 12 & -20 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}$$<br>The table shows four values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. Which of the following equations represents this relationship?","options":{"A":"$24x+6y=28$","B":"$24x+6y=168$","C":"$6x+24y=28$","D":"$6x+24y=168$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q05","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q05","label":"27","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$x+y+z=53$<br><br>The given equation relates the number of miles, $x$, that a cyclist biked on Monday, the number of miles, $y$, the cyclist biked on Tuesday, and the number of miles, $z$, that the cyclist biked on Wednesday in a certain week. If the cyclist biked 12 miles on Monday and 16 miles on Tuesday, how many miles did the cyclist bike on Wednesday?","options":{"A":"12","B":"24","C":"25","D":"36"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-A-M1-Q17","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAY-INT-A-M1-Q17","label":"28","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. The linear relationship between $x$ and $y$ can be represented by an equation written in the form $Ax + By = C$, where $A$, $B$, and $C$ are constants. What is the value of $\\frac{A}{B}$?","figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Table with columns x and y. Rows: x = -2, y = 19; x = 0, y = 31; x = 2, y = 43."}]},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q17","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-B-M1-Q17","label":"29","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"On January 1, 2000, the population of a town was $26{,}257$ and on January 1, 2010, the population was $26{,}858$. The equation $10x + 26{,}257 = 26{,}858$ describes this situation. Which of the following is the best interpretation of $x$ in this context?","options":{"A":"The total increase in population between 2000 and 2010","B":"The projected population of the town 10 years after 2010","C":"The average increase per year of the population between 2000 and 2010","D":"The percentage by which the population of the town increased each year between 2000 and 2010"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025JUN-INT-B-M2-Q02","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025JUN-INT-B-M2-Q02","label":"30","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"If the equations $-9x + y = 17$ and $9x + y = 17$ are graphed in the $xy$-plane, at what point $(x, y)$ do the graphs intersect?","options":{"A":"$(0, 17)$","B":"$(0, 9)$","C":"$(9, 0)$","D":"$(17, 0)$"}}]}